  "memories": [
    {
      "title": "Multi-Country Multilingual Telephony Architecture",
      "category": "telephony",
      "summary": "Automated country detection, language resolution, and engine alignment across 33+ countries for LiveKit voice agents",
      "tags": [
        "antigravity/memoria"
      ],
      "bodyExcerpt": "Multi-Country Multilingual Telephony Architecture [!NOTE] Automated country detection, language resolution, and engine alignment across 33+ countries for LiveKit voice agents Solucion Tecnica Implemented FastMCP tool resolve caller country language in livekit-mcp and calibrated lkt voice agent pipeline across 33+ countries. Inbound vs Outbound Telephony Quirks (Learned in Execution) 1. Inbound DID vs Caller Number Discrepancy: - In inbound calls, meta payload.get(\"phone number\") is the dialed DID (trunk number, e.g. +919484959268 ), NOT the customer's phone number! - Guarding entrypoint resolution with is inbound hint : Never pre-resolve caller country from phone number on inbound calls. - The actual caller number is extracted from the LiveKit SIP participant upon connect ( sip +39800957032 ). 2. Caller Resolution Overwrite Protection: - Removed if not call state.get(\"caller country\"): guard when participants join. The participant's caller-ID is the source of truth and must always resolve country and language. 3. Voice Overrides for Non-English Telephony: - When a caller's country language is non-English (e.g. Italian it , Spanish es , German de ), the regional Cartesia voice from the country catalog takes priority over default English voices (e.g. Arushi). 4. India Catalog Entry: - Added India ( IN , +91 , en-IN , Arushi voice 95d51f79-c397-46f9-b49a-23763d3eaa2d , Asia/Kolkata ) to COUNTRY CATALOG . Proyecto: [[lkt]]",
      "relPath": "Antigravity/Memoria/Multi-Country Multilingual Telephony Architecture.md",
      "updated": "2026-11-18"
    }
  ],
